    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "opening a new account sounds okay but they'll probably just see that as a sign i'm onto them and ramp up the pressure. i need more than just a complaint to the cfpb, i need a way to move my money more discreetly. are there any specific types of accounts or ways of transferring funds that don't trigger these 'liquidation' flags? i need to be able to get my savings out in pieces so they don't notice a massive drain and freeze everything before i'm ready.",
